            <title>[LU-21128] TCU: stale negative dentry for .Trash entries on other clients after delete (no cache invalidation)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21128</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reproduced on hardware.&lt;/b&gt; AI400X3i HA pair vm00/vm01, b_es7_0 2.16.0-ddn63 (702f1d2). Found by &lt;tt&gt;sanity-tcu.sh&lt;/tt&gt; test_81 (TCU, EX-428), using two mounts (&lt;tt&gt;/mnt/lustre&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;/mnt/lustre2&lt;/tt&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
echo x &amp;gt; $DIR/d/f
ls $DIR2/d/.Trash
# mount 2 looks up the virtual .Trash (empty)
rm $DIR/d/f # mount 1 deletes; the object goes to trash
ls $DIR2/d/.Trash/f
ls: cannot access &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;'/mnt/lustre2/d/.Trash/f'&lt;/span&gt;: No such file or directory&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;{{}}&lt;br/&gt;
The second client keeps a negative or readdir-cached view of the virtual &lt;tt&gt;.Trash&lt;/tt&gt; directory. Moving the object into the trash does not revoke any lock that protects that view. &lt;tt&gt;.Trash&lt;/tt&gt; is virtual (built from the trash index by pFID), so no LDLM lock covers its contents on the parent directory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Samerootcause%2CseenafterMDTrestart"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Same root cause, seen after MDT restart&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;After failing over MDT0000 and re-enabling TCU, &lt;tt&gt;ls $dir/.Trash&lt;/tt&gt; kept returning ENOENT on the client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The objects were present in &lt;tt&gt;.lustre/.ltrash&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The error cleared only after &lt;tt&gt;echo 3 &amp;gt; drop_caches&lt;/tt&gt; plus &lt;tt&gt;lru_size=clear&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Impact"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Impact&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On multi-client systems, users on other nodes cannot see or restore their files until their caches happen to expire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Expected"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Expected&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A delete into the trash, an unrm and a purge should invalidate &lt;tt&gt;.Trash&lt;/tt&gt; lookup and readdir caches on all clients. For example:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;take an UPDATE/LOOKUP ibits lock on the &lt;tt&gt;.Trash&lt;/tt&gt; virtual FID and cancel it on change, or&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;do not cache &lt;tt&gt;.Trash&lt;/tt&gt; entries at all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Test"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Test&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;sanity-tcu.sh&lt;/tt&gt; test_81: ".Trash cache coherency between clients".&lt;/p&gt;</description>
